WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:04.938
Bartering, part seven. A material day: the refresh dealt the ship material list.

2
00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:12.008
This sailor is building two Caravel parts, the Upgraded Plating and the Mayna Cannon, and keeps Level 3 and 4 goods at Port Epheria to hand over.

3
00:00:12.008 --> 00:00:16.154
Click "A material". The tab now reads the ship material list instead of the trade goods.

4
00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:23.591
The material list is one of the game’s forty-one material layouts, M1 to M41. Name it, and every island on it is known.

5
00:00:23.591 --> 00:00:29.157
Open Barter Information in the game, on the ship material list, and take a screenshot of the whole window.

6
00:00:29.248 --> 00:00:32.172
Paste it here, or click the box and choose the file.

7
00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:39.285
Each row paying a ship material is read and matched against what that island deals.

8
00:00:39.303 --> 00:00:43.944
The window’s head is read too: the Parley and your Total Barters. The app offers to write them in.

9
00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:45.424
Answer them.

10
00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:52.088
Seven islands fit three layouts. The bar says which island tells them apart, so read one more page.

11
00:00:52.088 --> 00:00:53.650
The second page.

12
00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:05.045
Layout M37. It agrees at every island read, and its other islands are filled in from the layout.

13
00:01:05.045 --> 00:01:09.045
The materials wanted: everything on this list your builds are short of, with how many.

14
00:01:09.045 --> 00:01:13.399
Pure Pearl Crystal: two islands today you can trade with, and the Parley it costs.

15
00:01:13.399 --> 00:01:19.060
Moon Scale Plywood: no island today deals it for a good you hold. Those are kept on the list and said plainly.

16
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:28.679
"The islands" lists who deals a material today, best payers first: the good each takes, how many times a day, and what you hold of it. And the ones you cannot do today, because the give is not held.

17
00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:37.899
How to sail it: for the wants and then home, or every island you can trade with; the island order; vouchers; quests on the way; and whether goods stored at another harbour are fetched on the way.

18
00:01:37.899 --> 00:01:42.703
And what comes of it: how many of each want this refresh brings, and how many are still wanted after.

19
00:01:42.703 --> 00:01:44.598
What nothing on this list deals is said too.

20
00:01:44.598 --> 00:01:50.501
The islands, the trades, the harbour call to load the Level 3s from Port Epheria, the hold, the time and the Parley.

21
00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:53.876
The material book shows all forty-one layouts, with what each one pays.

22
00:01:53.876 --> 00:01:57.162
Open M37, today’s, island by island.

23
00:01:57.352 --> 00:02:00.490
The To Get screen reads the same board. Open To Get.

24
00:02:01.243 --> 00:02:08.518
Today’s board: on the material list, layout M37 — what it deals toward your list today, island by island, and what each brings.

25
00:02:08.518 --> 00:02:11.051
Tick an island off when you have traded there.

26
00:02:11.051 --> 00:02:13.922
The islands that cannot be done today are folded below.

27
00:02:13.922 --> 00:02:18.620
"Sail it on the Barter tab" hands this board to the Barter tab, and the run is planned the same way.

28
00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:24.990
A refresh deals the material list or the trade goods, never both. Reading one puts down the other. Next, a short trip.
